{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649258",
      "title": "CSS Styling & Dynamic Styling",
      "sourceHash": "27b17fcae74ba8093f11246eb3f37375a2db1dedacacce325afa1060f9382ac1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 1.68,
          "en": "So, now that we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.68,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "how to render content conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 8.91,
          "en": "let's talk about styling and, most importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.91,
          "end": 13.29,
          "en": "about dynamic styling of HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.29,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "Because at the moment here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "we can select different tabs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 20.28,
          "en": "but, of course, we got no visual indicator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 23.13,
          "en": "about which tab is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.13,
          "end": 25.53,
          "en": "I mean, of course, we can tell by the content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.53,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "but it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 29.34,
          "en": "if the selected tab would be highlighted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 31.173,
          "en": "and that's currently not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 35.25,
          "en": "Now, we could achieve this by setting a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.25,
          "end": 37.653,
          "en": "on the button that was selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "And in React, you can set a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 44.943,
          "en": "by using the className prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.35,
          "end": 48.12,
          "en": "And that of course might be a bit strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.12,
          "end": 50.67,
          "en": "because in regular HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.67,
          "end": 54.987,
          "en": "you would use the class attribute instead, not className.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 58.2,
          "en": "Well, that's JSX-specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.2,
          "end": 62.16,
          "en": "and thankfully, most attributes, like id and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.16,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "are the same in JSX and HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "But for the class attribute, it's actually different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 72.99,
          "en": "And in JSX, you need to use className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.99,
          "end": 75.243,
          "en": "if you want to add a class to a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.2,
          "end": 81.15,
          "en": "But with that, we could add the active class to the button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.15,
          "end": 86.15,
          "en": "because that is a class I prepared in the index.css file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.16,
          "end": 88.26,
          "en": "In there, you'll find this rule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.26,
          "end": 90.753,
          "en": "which uses the active class for styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.1,
          "end": 93.12,
          "en": "So, if you add this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.12,
          "end": 96.99000000000001,
          "en": "you will see that all buttons are marked as active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.99000000000001,
          "end": 100.83,
          "en": "which of course is not really the result we want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 104.013,
          "en": "but we can at least see that we can style them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.45,
          "end": 106.71000000000001,
          "en": "But, now, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.71000000000001,
          "end": 110.7,
          "en": "the goal is to set this dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.7,
          "end": 113.31,
          "en": "And to set this dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 115.68,
          "en": "we could accept a new prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 119.913,
          "en": "which could be named isSelected, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 122.67,
          "en": "Again, the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 125.04,
          "en": "but, of course, the name should describe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.04,
          "end": 129.03,
          "en": "which kind of value this prop will hold.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.03,
          "end": 131.58,
          "en": "And here, we could expect to get a boolean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 134.25,
          "en": "which is true if this button is selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.25,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "so if it was clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 138.513,
          "en": "or false if it's currently not selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 143.04,
          "en": "And then we can set the className dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.04,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "again, by using these curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 147.96,
          "en": "which we always use if we need some dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.96,
          "end": 150.54,
          "en": "or JavaScript-based value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.54,
          "end": 153.333,
          "en": "And here, we could use a ternary expression again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.29,
          "end": 158.85,
          "en": "Because, just as we can output content conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.85,
          "end": 162.42000000000002,
          "en": "with ternary expressions and some other approaches,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.42000000000002,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "we can also set attributes conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 171.15,
          "en": "And here, we can set is className either to active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.15,
          "end": 173.253,
          "en": "if isSelected is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.45,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "or to an empty string, or undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 182.853,
          "en": "both is valid if this is currently not selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 187.65,
          "en": "so that this button has no class if it's not selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.65,
          "end": 190.473,
          "en": "but it has the active class if it is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.94,
          "end": 194.34,
          "en": "But, for this code here to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.34,
          "end": 198.45,
          "en": "we, of course, must make sure that we do pass a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.45,
          "end": 202.953,
          "en": "to this TabButton component for this isSelected prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.36,
          "end": 206.37,
          "en": "Hence, back in the App component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.37,
          "end": 208.383,
          "en": "where we're using the TabButton,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.22,
          "end": 214.22,
          "en": "we now need to add this second prop, this isSelected prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.25,
          "end": 217.65,
          "en": "and set it equal to a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.65,
          "end": 221.82,
          "en": "And this value, of course, also is derived dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.82,
          "end": 224.13,
          "en": "because it is based on our state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "on this selectedTopic state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 228.72,
          "en": "Because, when that state changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.72,
          "end": 231.03,
          "en": "the App component executes again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.03,
          "end": 234.423,
          "en": "and therefore these TabButtons are re-evaluated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.297,
          "end": 238.75,
          "en": "So therefore, here, we can use our selectedTopic state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.24,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "and check if it's equal to components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "because I'm on the Components button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.05,
          "end": 248.94,
          "en": "And this will yield true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.94,
          "end": 253.32,
          "en": "if selectedTopic is equal to this components identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.32,
          "end": 255.063,
          "en": "and false otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 259.74,
          "en": "And with that, we're then passing that true or false value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.74,
          "end": 261.723,
          "en": "to this isSelected prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 264.3,
          "en": "So, we can also copy that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.3,
          "end": 268.47,
          "en": "and add that to all the other TabButtons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.47,
          "end": 271.26,
          "en": "though, of course, on the second TabButton,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.26,
          "end": 273.65999999999997,
          "en": "this should be equal to jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.65999999999997,
          "end": 276.3,
          "en": "because this is the JSX button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 279.483,
          "en": "and I'll reformat the code to make it a bit easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.38,
          "end": 282,
          "en": "Here, for the third button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282,
          "end": 285.24,
          "en": "we wanna check for equality to props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 285.24,
          "end": 287.64,
          "en": "And for the last button, which is about State,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.64,
          "end": 290.58299999999997,
          "en": "we wanna check for equality to this identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.68,
          "end": 294.48,
          "en": "If we save this now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.48,
          "end": 297.48,
          "en": "you see that if I reload, nothing is selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.48,
          "end": 300.27,
          "en": "but if I click Components, this is selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.27,
          "end": 304.65,
          "en": "for JSX, that is selected, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.65,
          "end": 307.26,
          "en": "So, now, we got that visual feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.26,
          "end": 311.217,
          "en": "by conditionally setting that CSS className.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}